    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/how-to-apply/": {
      "title": "How toapply",
      "description": "How to apply | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login How to apply We appreciate the effort and commitment involved in making a job application and want to make sure you have a positive experience when applying for a role with us. Your application Your assessment Disability Confident Leader Accessibility Armed Forces Scheme Your application We shortlist our candidates against the criteria on the person specification section of the job description. We recommend that you address how you meet the person specification as part of your application. Try to do this by making sure that your application draws on your experience to provide relevant examples – this doesn’t always need to be from employment experience. If you believe that you could add value to our organisation but don’t meet all of the essential criteria for the role, we would still love to hear from you. You can contact the recruiter to discuss the value you could bring to our organisation. We will keep you updated on the progress of your application with us throughout the process. Your assessment Our process is tailored to the role that we’re recruiting, and we measure our success by the impact we make, so expect to bring your real-life skills into the recruitment process. From competency-based interviews, to teaching sessions and interactive assessments, this varies on the type of role you apply for, meaning that you will get the chance to show us exactly what you’re brilliant at doing. At interview, you will be asked to bring proof of your right to work in the UK, along with evidence of any relevant qualifications. Disability Confident Leader We are a Disability Confident Leader, and you will have opportunity as part of your application to let us know if you would like your application to be considered under the Disability Confident scheme. Where we have indicated that a role will be part of the scheme, a candidate who is disabled / has a long-term health condition and who meets the essential criteria for a vacancy will be offered an interview. For vacancies with a high volume of applications, only those who demonstrate they best meet the criteria will be offered an interview under the scheme. Read our Guidance and FAQs for Candidates who have a Disability or Long-term Health Condition before making an application as we can provide adjustments to ensure that candidates with a disability or those with a long-term health condition can participate on equal terms with non-disabled candidates. Accessibility We have a range of website accessibility options available on the right-hand side of the page. If you have any specific accessibility requests or would like to discuss reasonable adjustments, please do not hesitate to get in touch. Armed Forces Scheme We are committed to giving support to members of the Armed Forces and veterans through our work on the Armed Forces Covenant and through our receipt of the Employer Recognition Scheme Gold Award. The aim of our Armed Forces Guaranteed Interview Scheme is to ensure that any members of the Armed Forces and veterans are not disadvantaged through the application process. Those who would like to have their application considered under the scheme will have opportunity to indicate this as part of their application. Your application We shortlist our candidates against the criteria on the person specification section of the job description. We recommend that you address how you meet the person specification as part of your application. Try to do this by making sure that your application draws on your experience to provide relevant examples – this doesn’t always need to be from employment experience. If you believe that you could add value to our organisation but don’t meet all of the essential criteria for the role, we would still love to hear from you. You can contact the recruiter to discuss the value you could bring to our organisation. We will keep you updated on the progress of your application with us throughout the process. Your assessment Our process is tailored to the role that we’re recruiting, and we measure our success by the impact we make, so expect to bring your real-life skills into the recruitment process. From competency-based interviews, to teaching sessions and interactive assessments, this varies on the type of role you apply for, meaning that you will get the chance to show us exactly what you’re brilliant at doing. At interview, you will be asked to bring proof of your right to work in the UK, along with evidence of any relevant qualifications. Disability Confident Leader We are a Disability Confident Leader, and you will have opportunity as part of your application to let us know if you would like your application to be considered under the Disability Confident scheme. Where we have indicated that a role will be part of the scheme, a candidate who is disabled / has a long-term health condition and who meets the essential criteria for a vacancy will be offered an interview. For vacancies with a high volume of applications, only those who demonstrate they best meet the criteria will be offered an interview under the scheme. Read our Guidance and FAQs for Candidates who have a Disability or Long-term Health Condition before making an application as we can provide adjustments to ensure that candidates with a disability or those with a long-term health condition can participate on equal terms with non-disabled candidates. Accessibility We have a range of website accessibility options available on the right-hand side of the page. If you have any specific accessibility requests or would like to discuss reasonable adjustments, please do not hesitate to get in touch. Armed Forces Scheme We are committed to giving support to members of the Armed Forces and veterans through our work on the Armed Forces Covenant and through our receipt of the Employer Recognition Scheme Gold Award. The aim of our Armed Forces Guaranteed Interview Scheme is to ensure that any members of the Armed Forces and veterans are not disadvantaged through the application process. Those who would like to have their application considered under the scheme will have opportunity to indicate this as part of their application. Join us Together, we support a learning community of more than 39,000 people, providing vital expertise and leadership. We provide the foundation for engaging learning experiences and excellent research, and the opportunity to pursue a wide range of rewarding careers. If you have the vision and ambition to make a vital contribution to the future of Manchester Met, we look forward to hearing from you. Get in touch If you have any questions or require support with your application then please do not hesitate to get in touch with us at: manmetjobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/professorial/professorial-campaign": {
      "title": "Transform liveswith us",
      "description": "Transform lives with us | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Manchester Metropolitan University Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Manchester Metropolitan University Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professional opportunities Login Transform lives with us Join us and shape the future, through your teaching and research - because together, we can achieve breakthroughs that matter. Our research community at Manchester Metropolitan At Manchester Met, our research is at the heart of how we transform lives. From our home in the centre of Manchester – a city renowned for innovation – we’re making an impact that reaches across the UK and around the world. With research spanning four faculties and two flagship institutes – the Institute for Children’s Futures and the Institute of Sport – you’ll join a collaborative, diverse community where ideas thrive. Supported by world-class facilities and inspiring colleagues, you can push boundaries and turn ideas into real-world breakthroughs. With robust finances, we’re continually investing in our people, spaces and research environment – giving you and your team the opportunity and freedom to make an impact and transform lives with us. Find out about our research community Welcome from Professor Steve Rothberg Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor We are proud to be an inclusive community of over 5,100 staff and 44,000 students, united by a shared ambition: to make a real difference – transforming lives and helping partners across public, private, and charity sectors build sustainable futures. Excellence defines our community – in education and research. 90% of our research impact is world-leading or internationally excellent (REF2021), we hold the TEF Gold Award (2023–27), rank top 10 for student experience (NSS 2025), and no.1 for colleague experience (Inspire HE 2024/25). Through achievements like these, we are now Times and Sunday Times Modern University of the Year 2026. Manchester Metropolitan is a place where great ideas are nurtured, collaborations flourish, and careers reach new heights. We’re entering the third year of a five-year campaign to recruit 100 new professors. Together with our internal promotions, our new professors are already bringing senior leadership to advance education and research while upholding our values. If you are passionate about education and research, with a track record of success and a commitment to support colleagues, perhaps in a team you lead, we want to hear from you. Belong to a community of innovators Transforming lives together through education and research We’re Manchester Met proud - ambitious, innovative, and collaborative, using our world-class facilities and diverse expertise to be a force for good. Our research community is growing stronger every year, with increased support and investment enabling our teams to tackle ambitious projects and make real-world impact. Research funding has grown by 50% in just three years. And we’ve achieved a new ‘best’ with research awards of almost £30m last year, so we can keep making a difference. Recent highlights include: £3.8m from AHRC for the Robotics Living Lab £1m from the MRC for Parkinson’s research £1m from EPSRC for facial prosthetics Through partnerships with communities, businesses, industry and other institutions, we’re tackling the grand challenges of our time. Read our latest research news Our research is focused on five life-changing missions : Tackling inequalities Building cohesive communities and helping shape a more caring, just and inclusive society: locally, national and globally. Championing creative excellence Harnessing imagination to drive creativity, bringing architecture, art, design, fashion, media and performance together. Leading sustainability Driving innovative solutions for a greener and more sustainable future through advances in science and engineering practice and policy. Transforming health Enabling people to start well, live well and age well with innovative research and transformative healthcare. Driving economic growth Advancing skills, knowledge and digital technology to build inclusive and sustainable economic growth and innovation, shaped by industry. Read some of our impact stories Your career , our investment Once you join, we invest in you. You’ll have autonomy in an environment designed to unlock your potential, with a competitive salary, outstanding benefits package, and options for part-time working. Join us and discover a career with meaning—where your research can be forever bold, innovative and life-changing every day. Explore our rewards and benefits Our faculties Arts and Humanities Creative, diverse, and future-focused. Home to Manchester School of Art, Fashion Institute, and School of Architecture (ranked 5th in the world). Collaborate in world-class facilities and shape culture and society. Find out more Business and Law Globally connected, socially responsible, and entrepreneurial. A renowned triple-accredited Business School and a pioneering Law School. Influence workplaces, transform communities, and make a global impact. Find out more Health and Education Proud to be one of the region’s providers of nursing and allied health professionals. Train the next generation, tackle real-world challenges, and innovate in healthcare and education. Find out more Science and Engineering Research-led and globally impactful. Work in state-of-the-art facilities and pioneer solutions in engineering, energy, sport, cybersecurity, and advanced materials. Find out more Join our research community Bring your ideas to life in a place that gives you the freedom, support and world-class facilities to achieve your ambitions. Be part of a fast-growing research environment where you can collaborate with other experts at the forefront of their fields and work with communities, business and industry to tackle the grand challenges of our time. To find out more about the role that you can play in our exciting future, meet some of faculty leaders below who are available for informal discussions. Faculty of Arts & Humanities – Professor Chris Fox, Faculty Director of Research View Profile Faculty of Business & Law – Professor Dominic Medway, Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor View Profile Faculty of Health & Education – Professor Mike Coldwell, Faculty Director of Research View Profile Faculty of Science & Engineering – Professor Mark Sterling, Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor View Profile Connect with us We’re halfway through our ambitious plans to recruit 100 international research professors – aligning global talent with our key research strengths and growth strategy. With a number of key appointments already in place from recent years, this is an exciting time to join our research community and become an integral part of our commitment to creating research with impact. Interested? Connect with us and let’s talk about working at Manchester Met, whether it’s just you or it’s your team, whether you’re ready to join us right now or in the future. Connect with Manchester Met Be part of Manchester Met . Be Manchester Met proud . Transform lives with us. Get in Touch Manchester Metropolitan University Ormond Building Manchester M15 6BX United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 2000 Connect with us Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
